import{_ as n,o as a,c as i,a2 as t}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const p=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 917 | Myriad-Rank Republican Civilizational Charter · Article 16 — The Knowledge-Return-Only Principle","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 917 | Myriad-Rank Republican Civilizational Charter · Article 16 — The Knowledge-Return-Only Principle","no":917,"module":5,"tags":["Charter","Article 16","Knowledge Return Only","Knowledge Sharing","Causal Protection"],"related":["87-Knowledge-Return-Only Principle","69-Technology Opening and Sharing Mechanism","84-Archaeology Agreement General Outline"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0917_模块5-第十六条-仅回传知识原则.md","filePath":"en/0917_模块5-第十六条-仅回传知识原则.md"}'),o={name:"en/0917_模块5-第十六条-仅回传知识原则.md"};function r(l,e,s,c,u,h){return a(),i("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[t('<h1 id="entry-917-myriad-rank-republican-civilizational-charter-·-article-16-—-the-knowledge-return-only-principle" tabindex="-1">Entry 917 | Myriad-Rank Republican Civilizational Charter · Article 16 — The Knowledge-Return-Only Principle <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-917-myriad-rank-republican-civilizational-charter-·-article-16-—-the-knowledge-return-only-principle" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 917 | Myriad-Rank Republican Civilizational Charter · Article 16 — The Knowledge-Return-Only Principle&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 5 · Civilization Final-Finalization Canonical Entries | Benchmark base: Documents 87, 69, 84</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-bring-back-only-knowledge-nothing-else" tabindex="-1">Introduction: bring back only knowledge, nothing else <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-bring-back-only-knowledge-nothing-else" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: bring back only knowledge, nothing else&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Article 15 says &quot;how to watch, how to move&quot;; Article 16 says &quot;what to bring back after watching.&quot; It stipulates: the only permitted product of cross-plane and time-tracing operations is knowledge — observations&#39; knowledge may be returned to the Alaya Network for Myriad Ranks to learn, but material, energy, beings, or fortune from the target plane may not be taken away, nor one&#39;s own causality implanted. This is the causal self-discipline axiom&#39;s final lock at the &quot;results&quot; link. Knowledge is an increment; the more it is shared, the more it grows; matter and causality are stock; taking one thing away disturbs a whole patch.</p><p>This article is from beginning to end placed under the six top-level axioms — the anti-predation axiom draws the bottom line, the republican axiom of Myriad Races establishes the subject, the collective-ascension axiom sets the direction, the causal self-discipline axiom guards the boundary, the law-first axiom preserves self-consistency; the five together constitute this article&#39;s insurmountable spiritual boundary.</p><p>Together with the previous five axioms, this article is also bound by Axiom 6 · Universal Equal Infinite Law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing and layabouts retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will not be eliminated by the times; strivers and Youth Supremes may superimpose more and higher levels of infinity; predation thus fundamentally loses meaning.</p><h2 id="i-jurisprudential-basis" tabindex="-1">I. Jurisprudential Basis <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-jurisprudential-basis" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. Jurisprudential Basis&quot;">​</a></h2><p>This article is based on the Knowledge-Return-Only Principle (Document 87), the Technology Opening and Sharing Mechanism (Document 69), and the Archaeology Agreement General Outline (Document 84). Its jurisprudence is: cross-plane operations&#39; legitimate purpose is seeking knowledge and mutual aid, not transport and predation. Returning knowledge network-wide both expands Myriad Ranks&#39; cognition and does not disturb the target plane&#39;s causality; while carrying back any material or energy establishes new causal entanglement between two planes, sowing seeds of future conflict and colonization.</p><h2 id="ii-normative-content-what-to-return-what-not-to-return" tabindex="-1">II. Normative Content: What to Return, What Not to Return <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-normative-content-what-to-return-what-not-to-return" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Normative Content: What to Return, What Not to Return&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Article 16 draws the return boundary:</p><ul><li><strong>May return</strong>: observed knowledge, laws, cultural records, technical principles, all entered into the Alaya Network for network-wide sharing;</li><li><strong>Forbidden to take</strong>: target plane&#39;s primordial matter, energy veins, individual beings, fortune crystals, law fragments;</li><li><strong>Forbidden to implant</strong>: do not implant one&#39;s own plane&#39;s people, objects, values into the target plane, do not &quot;make decisions&quot; for it;</li><li><strong>Exception channel</strong>: only when the target plane actively requests and its own clan self-government agrees, may the cross-plane aid procedure be followed, separately approved.</li></ul><h2 id="iii-scope" tabindex="-1">III. Scope <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-scope" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Scope&quot;">​</a></h2><p>This article applies to all cross-plane operation teams and individuals. Archaeological teams, diplomatic missions, cultivation tour groups apply equally. Seemingly harmless acts like &quot;casually taking an antique as a souvenir&quot; are equally forbidden — a souvenir is also stock transport. This article does not exclude broad knowledge sharing: on the contrary, returned knowledge is fully open to Myriad Ranks; this is precisely cross-plane operations&#39; true value.</p><h2 id="iv-consequences-of-violation" tabindex="-1">IV. Consequences of Violation <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-consequences-of-violation" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Consequences of Violation&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Privately carrying material or energy out of the target plane, secretly bringing back individual beings, implanting home-plane influence without consent, running plane colonization under the name of &quot;scholarship,&quot; all constitute unconstitutionality under this article. Consequences: brought-back items are forcibly returned or harmlessly disposed of, and the relevant knowledge-return qualification is suspended; those causing target-plane ecological or causal damage are pursued heavily under plane colonization (Article 1) and causal disturbance (Article 4).</p><h2 id="v-supervision-mechanism" tabindex="-1">V. Supervision Mechanism <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-supervision-mechanism" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Supervision Mechanism&quot;">​</a></h2><p>This article is executed by Alaya Network + multi-layer supervision: cross-plane entry and exit&#39;s material and energy carried amount is scanned and compared by anchor anchoring devices, excess immediately intercepted; returned knowledge&#39;s catalog is publicized network-wide, subject to each clan&#39;s supervision on &quot;whether private goods are hidden&quot;; the time-operation archive library records every operation&#39;s actual products for post-audit.</p><h2 id="vi-a-hand-returning-empty" tabindex="-1">VI. A Hand Returning Empty <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-a-hand-returning-empty" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI. A Hand Returning Empty&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Article 16&#39;s most moving picture is a hand returning empty. A cultivator walked through over a dozen other planes, and when leaving took nothing — no casually picked antique, no rare treasure, no stone wanting to keep as a souvenir, only returned with a belly full of learned knowledge. This knowledge is entered into the Alaya Network; Myriad Ranks henceforth have the wisdom of over a dozen more planes. Returning with empty hands looks like gaining nothing, but actually brings back the most precious thing, without leaving a wound on any plane. Knowledge-return-only makes the explorer&#39;s far journey a pure gift, not another gentle predation.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><p><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: knowledge copies at zero cost, material transport is expensive; returning only knowledge is the most economical exploration</p></li><li><p><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: this article directly blocks the old colonial road of &quot;looting things under the guise of exploration&quot;</p></li><li><p><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang-Luo-type protagonists loot wherever they go, carrying away piles of treasures; Heng Yuan Zhou brings back only knowledge, departing with empty hands, returning with a belly full of learning</p></li><li><p><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: returned knowledge is fully open to Myriad Ranks; exploration results belong to all</p></li><li><p><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: knowledge sharing makes every cross-plane exploration a civilizational cognitive increment</p></li><li><p><strong>Universal equal infinity</strong>: every being inherently possesses basic infinite power; the easygoing layabouts retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will not be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes may superimpose higher-level infinity; predation thus fundamentally loses meaning</p></li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The knowledge-return-only principle is the &quot;gentlemen&#39;s agreement&quot; Heng Yuan Zhou lays down for cross-plane exploration. It lets Myriad Ranks safely see every corner of the cosmos, without worrying any viewing turns into another colonization. Bring only wisdom, not a single inch of land — this is true civilizational confidence.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/87-仅回传知识原则.html">Entry 87 · Knowledge-Return-Only Principle</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/69-技术开放与共享机制.html">Entry 69 · Technology Opening and Sharing Mechanism</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/84-考古协议总纲.html">Entry 84 · Archaeology Agreement General Outline</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/916_模块5-第十五条-先观测后有限干涉.html">Entry 916 · Article 15 Observe First, Then Limited Intervention</a></li></ul>',25)])])}const g=n(o,[["render",r]]);export{p as __pageData,g as default};
